From: Panurus maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 8/10] toolbox: distinct challenges for every accumulator pair

___schwartz_zippel_accumulate2 drew 2 * M challenges from (seed, dom) inside
its loop over the lambda / 2 accumulator pairs, so every pair got the same
challenges and the step gave 2 independent Schwartz-Zippel tests whatever
lambda (lazer-crypto/lazer#24). It now draws a lambda x M matrix once and
pair i uses rows 2i and 2i + 1, as _schwartz_zippel_int in lnp-quad-eval.c
and the z3/z4 accumulators do.

Applied to the toolbox copy in src/lin-proofs.c, which the lin_* proofs
run. It changes the transcript; proof sizes do not change.

Panurus-local patch, applied by `make lazer-install` (lazer.mk).

diff --git a/src/lin-proofs.c b/src/lin-proofs.c
index 636b1e8..f6421de 100644
--- a/src/lin-proofs.c
+++ b/src/lin-proofs.c
@@ -2325,18 +2325,23 @@ ___schwartz_zippel_accumulate2 (
   polyring_srcptr Rq = quad_eval->ring;
   int_srcptr q = polyring_get_mod (Rq);
   const unsigned int log2q = polyring_get_log2q (Rq);
-  INTVEC_T (V, 2 * M, Rq->q->nlimbs);
+  INTVEC_T (V, lambda * M, Rq->q->nlimbs);
   intvec_t subv1, subv2;
   unsigned int i;
 
   DEBUG_PRINTF (DEBUG_PRINT_FUNCTION_ENTRY, "%s begin", __func__);
 
-  intvec_get_subvec (subv1, V, 0, M, 1);
-  intvec_get_subvec (subv2, V, M, M, 1);
+  /*
+   * a lambda x M challenge matrix, rows 2i and 2i+1 for the i-th pair of
+   * accumulators: drawing 2M values from (seed, dom) for every pair gave all
+   * lambda/2 pairs the same challenges (panurus patch, lazer-crypto/lazer#24)
+   */
+  intvec_urandom (V, q, log2q, seed, dom);
 
   for (i = 0; i < lambda / 2; i++)
     {
-      intvec_urandom (V, q, log2q, seed, dom);
+      intvec_get_subvec (subv1, V, (2 * i) * M, M, 1);
+      intvec_get_subvec (subv2, V, (2 * i + 1) * M, M, 1);
 
       ___schwartz_zippel_accumulate (R2i[i], r1i[i], r0i[i], R2primei,
                                      r1primei, r0primei, M, subv1, u0, u1, u2,
